---
layout: layout.njk
title: "Habibi — An agent of your own."
description: "An open-source personal agent in the making. Explore the interface direction, local-first memory, and the boundaries of encrypted sync."
pagination:
  data: locales
  size: 1
  alias: locale
permalink: "{{ locale | homePath }}"
---
<main id="main" class="wrap">
  <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-heading">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">{{ dgettext("marketing", "Open-source personal agent · In development") }}</p>
      <h1 id="hero-heading">{{ dgettext("marketing", "An agent of your own.") }}</h1>
    </div>
    <div class="hero-intro">
      <p>{{ dgettext("marketing", "Habibi is a personal agent in the making. A place for notes, plans, and conversations, designed around your life rather than a blank chat box.") }}</p>
      <a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/pepicrft/habibi" rel="noopener noreferrer">{{ dgettext("marketing", "Follow the build") }} <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <figure class="interface-study" aria-labelledby="study-caption">
    <div class="study-stage">
      <div class="study-note">
        <p class="eyebrow">{{ dgettext("marketing", "The idea") }}</p>
        <h2>{{ dgettext("marketing", "A conversation, with context.") }}</h2>
        <p>{{ dgettext("marketing", "Something you saved becomes something you can use. The answer keeps a path back to the original note.") }}</p>
        <p class="study-instruction">{{ dgettext("marketing", "Open the source below the answer.") }} <span aria-hidden="true">↘</span></p>
      </div>
      <div class="conversation">
        <div class="conversation-heading">{% include "companion.njk" %}<span>habibi</span><span class="conversation-label">{{ dgettext("marketing", "Interface study") }}</span></div>
        <p class="message-user"><span class="visually-hidden">{{ dgettext("marketing", "You:") }} </span>{{ dgettext("marketing", "What was that little place Maya wanted to try?") }}</p>
        <div class="message-agent">
          <p class="message-author">Habibi</p>
          <p>{{ dgettext("marketing", "Olive & Fig. You saved it after your walk together.") }}</p>
          <div class="place-card">
            <div class="place-card-heading"><span class="place-symbol" aria-hidden="true">↗</span><div><h3>{{ dgettext("marketing", "Olive & Fig") }}</h3><p>{{ dgettext("marketing", "For lunch with Maya") }}</p></div></div>
            <details class="source-note">
              <summary>{{ dgettext("marketing", "From your own notes") }} <span class="details-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
              <div class="source-content"><p class="source-title">{{ dgettext("marketing", "After our walk") }}</p><blockquote>{{ dgettext("marketing", "Maya mentioned Olive & Fig for lunch next time. Somewhere with a little courtyard.") }}</blockquote></div>
            </details>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="study-followup"><span aria-hidden="true">↳</span> {{ dgettext("marketing", "A note, not a guess.") }}</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <figcaption id="study-caption"><span>{{ dgettext("marketing", "Remembering a place") }}</span><span>{{ dgettext("marketing", "Interface concept, not a released app.") }}</span></figcaption>
  </figure>

  <section class="editorial-section" id="about" aria-labelledby="about-heading">
    <div><p class="eyebrow">{{ dgettext("marketing", "About") }}</p><h2 id="about-heading">{{ dgettext("marketing", "More than a transcript.") }}</h2></div>
    <div class="section-copy">
      <p>{{ dgettext("marketing", "The app we’re working toward can turn a conversation into a plan, a list you can change, or a useful reminder. Answers should have sources. Actions should be reviewable.") }}</p>
      <p>{{ dgettext("marketing", "Memory and search are intended to live on your devices. Longer-running work can go to a computer you pair, with access you explicitly grant. These are design goals; the mobile app isn’t built yet.") }}</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="editorial-section" id="privacy" aria-labelledby="privacy-heading">
    <div><p class="eyebrow">{{ dgettext("marketing", "Privacy") }}</p><h2 id="privacy-heading">{{ dgettext("marketing", "Who can read what.") }}</h2><p class="section-aside">{{ dgettext("marketing", "The intended boundaries, without the fine print.") }}</p></div>
    <div class="privacy-notes">
      <article><h3>{{ dgettext("marketing", "Your devices") }}</h3><p>{{ dgettext("marketing", "Your devices hold the vault key and encrypt content before sync. Local memory and search are planned for the app; the reference client already encrypts synced objects.") }}</p></article>
      <article><h3>{{ dgettext("marketing", "Your AI provider") }}</h3><p>{{ dgettext("marketing", "The app is being designed to contact your chosen provider directly. That provider can read the prompts and context you send. Its retention policies apply; encrypted sync does not hide prompts from it.") }}</p></article>
      <article><h3>{{ dgettext("marketing", "The sync service") }}</h3><p>{{ dgettext("marketing", "The prototype stores ciphertext, not your content keys or provider credentials. It still sees account and sync metadata, including object sizes and request timing. This is not anonymity.") }}</p></article>
      <details class="recovery-note"><summary>{{ dgettext("marketing", "What if I lose my devices?") }}<span class="details-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="details-content"><p>{{ dgettext("marketing", "You need both a separately kept recovery key and an exported encrypted recovery bundle. The reference client can export the bundle; the mobile recovery interface isn’t built. Without a remaining device or both parts of the recovery kit, the operator cannot recover your content.") }}</p></div></details>
      <p class="privacy-caveat">{{ dgettext("marketing", "Experimental and unaudited. These boundaries are not a security guarantee.") }}</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="editorial-section building-section" id="building" aria-labelledby="building-heading">
    <div><p class="eyebrow">{{ dgettext("marketing", "In development") }}</p><h2 id="building-heading">{{ dgettext("marketing", "Where things stand.") }}</h2></div>
    <div class="section-copy">
      <p>{{ dgettext("marketing", "The first piece is a ciphertext-only sync prototype, built with Elixir, Postgres, and S3-compatible storage. There’s no mobile app to download and no launch date yet.") }}</p>
      <div class="project-links"><a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/pepicrft/habibi" rel="noopener noreferrer">{{ dgettext("marketing", "Read the source") }} <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="text-link" href="{{ locale | homePath }}changelog/">{{ dgettext("marketing", "Changelog") }} <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
    </div>
  </section>
</main>
